      "notes": "Period report transcription. Level and climb results reduced to NACA standard conditions. Shaft power comes from Wright Field power curves dated 3 December 1943. Phase and configuration stay with each series."
    },
    {
      "id": "AAF-AN01-60JE1-STALLY",
      "aircraft": "North American P-51D/K manual reference",
      "report": "AN 01-60JE-1, Normal Operating Instructions, archived in the NTSB docket",
      "location": "Section II §15, printed p. 21, Stalling Speeds tables",
      "source": "https://data.ntsb.gov/Docket/Document/docBLOB?FileExtension=.PDF&FileName=P51D+Normal+Operating+Instructions-Master.PDF&ID=40206631",
      "notes": "Source-reported IAS by gross weight and configuration. The docket excerpt does not identify a flight run or serial number. A separate earlier April 1944 D-5 manual uses figures 24–25."
    },
    {
      "id": "AOPA-P51D-GEOMETRY",
      "aircraft": "North American P-51D representative geometry",
      "report": "AOPA Pilot, North American Aviation P-51D Mustang",
